# GD-2 (round 19): L §7.1 "Month-day literals (`04-30`, §3.1) are date literals here: they appear only in rows (a
# calendar's `yearly` list included), an anchored index's `from`, pins and asks, and a rule can't hold one
# (`LOAD-LITERAL`)": day_of(y, 04-30) in a def.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2026..2027
input file_by: monthday
input other: monthday
def d[y in yrs]: date = day_of(y, 04-30)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  file_by = 04-30
  other = 04-30
ask q: d[2026]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL a date in a rule; make it a version (m.tally:12)
